 Chapter~\ref{ch:overall} discusses the work as a whole. It opens with the outcome, that improved first-pass robot design is now achievable, and attributes it: the design factors that remove the rigid-body idealization, the improved BPA characterization, the tiered attachment and routing optimization, the sensory afferent database, and the new neuromechanical simulation tools. Its remaining subsections scope the future work these results enable for other researchers, from BPA characterization and routing expansion through database and simulation tooling to real-time neural control of the physical robot. Chapter~\ref{ch:conclusion} consolidates the principal contributions of the dissertation.
 
